{0 elpi}

This is the API reference for the [elpi] OCaml package.

{1 Public API}

{!module:Elpi} (library [elpi], findlib [-package elpi]) is the only
public, supported entry point: everything a host application needs to
embed the interpreter, drive it, and extend it with custom builtins,
data types and quotations lives under this one module (see the
{{:../embedding.html} Embedding and extending} chapter of the user
manual for a guided tour).

{1 Internal libraries}

The rest of this package's libraries are Elpi's own implementation, split
into separate dune libraries for internal build reasons:
{!module:Elpi_compiler}, {!module:Elpi_lexer_config}, {!module:Elpi_parser},
{!module:Elpi_runtime}, {!module:Elpi_trace_atd}, {!module:Trace_ppx},
{!module:Trace_ppx_runtime} and {!module:Elpi_util}. They are documented
here only because they are part of the same opam package; they are
{b not} a supported API, carry no compatibility guarantees across releases,
and a host application should never depend on them directly.
